        "original_id": "fbdd79d1-3250-5a2c-a11b-4b108cd6b871",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Robinsons, Pocari Sweat, Robinsons barley water\n- Companies: Britvic, Otsuka Pharmaceutical\n- People: Hugh Manning, Kathleen Harrison\n- Works: Mrs Thursday\n- Places: England, Japan, East Asia, Southeast Asia, Middle East\n- Topics: drink brands, sports drinks, TV commercials\n\nFacts:\n- Robinsons is an English fruit drink brand owned by Britvic.\n- Pocari Sweat is a Japanese sports drink manufactured by Otsuka Pharmaceutical.\n- Pocari Sweat was launched in 1980 and later became available in East Asia, Southeast Asia, and the Middle East.\n- In 1966, Hugh Manning starred with Kathleen Harrison in the TV series Mrs Thursday as a suave and imperturbable butler.\n- Hugh Manning later used a similar character in popular TV commercials endorsing Robinsons barley water.",
